   "title": "Downloads + requirements",
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Downloads + requirements\n\nClick a file name to download it. Put it in the folder shown (inside `ComfyUI/models/`).\n\n| Folder | File (click = download) | Size |\n|---|---|---|\n| `diffusion_models/` | [minimax_music3_dit_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-Music-3/resolve/main/diffusion_models/minimax_music3_dit_int8_convrot.safetensors) | 2.50 GB |\n| `text_encoders/` | [minimax_music3_text_encoder_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-Music-3/resolve/main/text_encoders/minimax_music3_text_encoder_pruned_int8_convrot.safetensors) | 9.20 GB |\n| `vae/` | [minimax_music3_dav.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-Music-3/resolve/main/vae/minimax_music3_dav.safetensors) | 0.22 GB |\n\nTotal: about 11.9 GB. All three are the Comfy-Org repackaged files. The template loads the fp16 DiT (4.91 GB); this workflow loads the int8 one, which the template's note lists \"for low VRAM\". The fp16 file was not run here.\n\n**VRAM:** 12 GB is the target. v1.0.0 (same files and settings) peaked at 11.3 GB (60 s) and 11.5 GB (120 s) on an RTX 3060 12 GB. v1.1.0 is **not verified on a 12 GB card**: on the 24 GB test card ComfyUI took 16.5 GiB (whole GPU) without a limit, and with `--reserve-vram 13.5` the ComfyUI process peaked at 11.2 GiB for the 163 s song (whole GPU 12.0 GiB, up to 1.1 GiB of it other programs).\n\n**Run on ComfyUI 0.45.3. No custom nodes.** The MiniMax Music 3 nodes are in core since ComfyUI 0.33.0 (PR #15570, August 2026), but that is not a tested minimum: this workflow was only run on 0.45.3 (v1.0.0 on 0.43.1). Older versions are not verified.\n\nLicence: MiniMax-Music3 Community License ([text](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-Music3/blob/main/LICENSE)): commercial use is allowed with conditions (show \"MiniMax-Music3\" in a commercial product; ask MiniMax above 20 million US dollars of yearly revenue; an acceptable use policy). The Comfy-Org repackage is tagged Apache-2.0.\n"
   ]
  },
